urname><given-names>HK</given-names></name><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name></person-group><etal/><article-title>Nonfebrile illness seizures: a unique seizure category?</article-title><source>Epilepsia</source><year>2005</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>952</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15946338</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B51"><label>51</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Kuturec</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Emoto</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Sofijanov</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><etal/><article-title>Febrile seizures: is the EEG a useful predictor of recurrences?</article-title><source>Clin.Pediatr.(Phila)</source><year>1997</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9007345</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B52"><label>52</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Warden</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Zibulewsky</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mace</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gold</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gausche-Hill</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation and management of febrile seizures in the out-of-hospital and emergency department settings</article-title><source>Ann Emerg Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12548271</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B53"><label>53</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>al Eissa</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lumbar puncture in the clinical evaluation of children with seizures associated with fever</article-title><source>Pediatr Emerg Care</source><year>1995</year><v